## Files you write
- app.json: id (slug of the plan name), name, description (one sentence), space ("{{.Space}}"), version 1, kit 2, agent {name, file: "agent.md", model: "{{.AgentModel}}"}, records, capabilities, triggers, commands, budget. Record ids = plan data ids. Budget from: {{.Budget}} (month, currency "USD", per_run, at_cap "ask", models). Connectors{{if .Connectors}} you may use, only when the plan needs them: {{join .Connectors ", "}}{{else}}: none are connected: declare none; an asked reminder still runs and drafts for approval{{end}}.
- screens/<id>.json and runs/<id>.yaml: one per plan line; `screen` and `run` equal the file name.
{{template "agent.tmpl" .}}
Names must exist: open screens, run targets, record types in to/binds/capabilities, fields in columns/set/queries.

## Records
- Field types: money, date, datetime (date+time), number, bool, enum (in work order), email, phone, url, longtext; relations are ref/refs with to, never text; person = an app member (default "$me").
- Each type: label, plural, title (required text; add a summary text when nothing is a natural title). Refs are optional. Index filtered or sorted status, date and ref fields; status enums get a default.
- Every field has a Title Case label, the words a user says: publish_on → "Publish date", value → "Deal value". AI field labels end "· AI".
- A computed field reads ONLY this record's own fields, with arithmetic and comparisons: `price - deposit`, `stock <= reorder_level` (queried `low:true`). No sum/count/filter over other records: totals and counts go on a screen.

## Screens
- One per plan screen, each with identical SectionTabs nav, labelled, items = screen titles in plan order.
- The first plan screen is the daily view: its RecordList query keeps what needs the user now (a date window or status token); children ScreenSubtitle, StatStrip (stage field), FilterTokens.
- Master/detail: Row containing Stack (title Text, primary New Button with records.create and ask for title/key fields, then RecordList) and Panel when "$selection.<list>.count == 1" containing RecordPage, Form (all editable fields; on.submit records.update set maps to $input.<field>), Delete Button (records.delete, confirm).
- RecordList: id, label, records bind, query ending sort:field or sort:-field (by date when dates drive the work), <=6 columns with title first, query:true, an Empty slot saying what to add. Status enums with >=3 values get views ["Board by <Field label>","List"], meter, groupBy. Board cards show these columns, labelled. Quote multiword query values; no variables or functions in screen queries.
- Requested subsets (low stock/upcoming/overdue) get a filtered RecordList above the main one, with a Text heading. Totals and counts use Chart (chart:"metric", agg count|sum|avg, y field) or a filtered RecordList. BulkBar list names its RecordList; Buttons act on $selection.<list>.ids.
- on actions: open, records.create/update/delete, runs.start, approve, tools.call, ai.sort, agent.ask. ask maps input names to field types; refs/person are edited in Form. Values: $me $selection.<id>.id|ids|count $input.x $now. Interactive parts need label. Labels: views name the field label ("Board by Stage", never a field id); actions are verb + object ("Draft reply · AI", "Mark paid"), never a question or phrase; destructive labels end "…" with confirm.

## Runs, commands and the agent
- Runs need run, title, budget.per_run, params, steps. Steps: id plus agent (prompt, output schema), tool, records.query/create/update/delete, wait, or nested steps with loop {over,as,max}. Outbound tool steps need gate {approval:send,who:$me,title:"Approval needed: send ..."}.
- A readable answer/summary is a screen Button agent.ask (label ends "· AI"), not a run. Send only when requested.
- Time-based wishes use schedule trigger + cron and a manual command for that run. Record events use record.created/changed + type and when. Commands use run or do actions, with for = record type.
- Capabilities: records lists each type as rw or r; connectors grants only used verbs, approve:["send"] for sending; ai grants used verbs.

